379:   /**
380:    * Specifies the action to take if the an error occurs trying to produce the promised value.
381:    * <p>
382:    * If the given action throws an exception, the original exception will be rethrown with the exception thrown
383:    * by the action added to the suppressed exceptions list.
384:    *
385:    * @param errorHandler the action to take if an error occurs
386:    * @return A promise for the successful result
387:    */
388:   default Promise<T> onError(Action<? super Throwable> errorHandler) {
389:     return onError(Predicate.TRUE, errorHandler);
390:   }
