1484:   /**
1485:    * Allows the execution of the promise to be deferred to a later time.
1486:    * <p>
1487:    * When the returned promise is subscribed to, the given {@code releaser} action will be invoked.
1488:    * The execution of {@code this} promise is deferred until the runnable given to the {@code releaser} is run.
1489:    * <p>
1490:    * It is generally more convenient to use {@link #throttled(Throttle)} or {@link #onYield(Runnable)} than this operation.
1491:    *
1492:    * @param releaser the action that will initiate the execution some time later
1493:    * @return a deferred promise
1494:    */
1495:   default Promise<T> defer(Action<? super Runnable> releaser) {
1496:     return transform(up -> down ->
1497:       Promise.async(innerDown ->
1498:         releaser.execute((Runnable) () -> innerDown.success(true))
1499:       ).then(v ->
1500:         up.connect(down)
1501:       )
1502:     );
1503:   }
